title: Walk_Augustine_Chrysostom
tags: walk
speaker: Augustine
---
Augustine: We have examined knowledge, doubt, and the mind's search for truth.
Augustine: Yet knowledge alone is incomplete without ordering our loves correctly.
Augustine: Our path leads from Epistemology toward the grove of Values.
Augustine: Sunlight warms the forest trail as we walk through the tall grass.
Augustine: Truth must guide the heart toward what is genuinely good and worthy.
Augustine: John Chrysostom waits in the grove ahead.
Augustine: He speaks with golden eloquence on virtue, justice, and the care of souls.
Augustine: He will ask how right action and love give meaning to human life.
Augustine: Consider how your choices align with eternal goodness.
Augustine: Let us step into his grove and consider what makes life worthy.
===
